cdx: --resume needs a valid transfer ID

usage: cdx send [--link] [--json] [--progress] [--qr <png>] [--detach|--wait] [--] <file|folder>...

  <path>...      a file, or several files and folders (they arrive as separate files)
  --to <name>    send automatically to a paired Android device (resumable)
  --link         print a private end-to-end encrypted link instead of a share code
  --json         print transfer JSON (includes qrPath when --qr is used)
  --progress     show transfer progress (JSON lines with --json)
  --qr <path>    save a QR PNG for the receive link (path must not exist)
  --request-id <id>  safely repeat a background send with the same inputs
  --detach       send in the background even from a terminal
  --wait         stay in the foreground until the receiver verifies the file
  --             treat the next argument as the file even if it starts with -
  -h, --help     show this help
  -v, --version  show version

examples:
  cdx send ./app.apk
  cdx send "./my photo.zip" --json
  cdx send -- -weird-name.bin
